    faqs: [
      { q: 'What are the different types of cannabis concentrates?', a: 'Cannabis concentrates include several distinct types based on their extraction method and consistency. Wax is soft and opaque, shatter is glassy and translucent, budder and badder are creamy, crumble is dry and crumbly, live resin is made from fresh-frozen plants for maximum terpene preservation, live rosin uses solventless extraction for purity, diamonds are crystalline THCA formations, and sauce combines diamonds with terpene-rich liquid. Each offers a different experience in terms of flavor, potency, and ease of use.' },
      { q: 'How much can I save on concentrate deals?', a: 'Concentrate deals typically offer savings of 15-30% off regular pricing, with deeper discounts available during multi-gram bundles and holiday sales. A standard gram of live resin that costs $50 at regular price might drop to $35-$40 on deal. Multi-gram bundles like three grams for $100 instead of $150 individually offer 33% savings. During major sales events like 4/20 or 7/10 (Dab Day), concentrate discounts can reach 40-50% off, making it an ideal time to stock up on your preferred products.' },
      { q: 'What is the best concentrate for beginners?', a: 'For beginners, live resin or wax with moderate THC levels around 60-70% are the most approachable concentrates. These products offer great flavor and a noticeable but not overwhelming experience. Avoid starting with diamonds or distillate, which can exceed 90% THC and may be uncomfortably intense for those without concentrate experience. A nectar collector or small dab pen is a good starter device since they are simpler to use than a full dab rig with a torch.' },
      { q: 'What is 7/10 and why is it important for concentrate deals?', a: 'July 10th, written as 7/10, is known as Dab Day or Oil Day in the cannabis community because the number 710 spells OIL when flipped upside down. It is the concentrate equivalent of 4/20 and is celebrated with the deepest concentrate discounts of the year. Dispensaries and concentrate brands offer special pricing, limited-edition extracts, and promotional events focused entirely on dabs and concentrates. If you are a concentrate enthusiast, 7/10 is the best day to stock up on your favorite products at the lowest prices.' },
      { q: 'How should I store concentrates I buy on deal?', a: 'Store concentrates in a cool, dark place in their original sealed containers or in airtight silicone or glass containers. Avoid heat and direct light, which degrade cannabinoids and terpenes over time. Refrigeration can extend shelf life but allow the product to reach room temperature before opening to prevent condensation. Most concentrates maintain their quality for three to six months with proper storage, with solventless products like rosin being the most sensitive to degradation and best consumed within one to two months of purchase.' },
    ],
